{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>You have seen that from heaven I spoke with you.</b> Because all Israel are witnesses in what they saw with their own eyes — the great signs and wonders from the beginning, the ten plagues of Egypt, through the end of the giving of the Torah — therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, reminded them: 'You have seen,' both at the beginning and at the end. For so in the passage of the covenant and the conditions He began and said: ״אתם ראיתם אשר עשיתי למצרים״, and now He says to them: ״אתם ראיתם כי מן השמים דברתי עמכם״ — for His glory was on Mount Sinai, and the speech was from heaven. And this has already been explained."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:01:42.347869411Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}